# 🎯 Feature #1: Smart Question Paper Builder (Drag & Drop)

## What It Does — Detailed Explanation

### The Problem Today

The current paper generation flow in [generate.html](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/templates/main/generate.html) works like this:

```
Class → Subject → Chapters → [View Questions] → Check/Uncheck → Generate
```

While functional, it has several UX limitations:

1. **No reordering** — Questions appear in the order they are in the DB. Teachers can't rearrange them
2. **No section grouping** — MCQ, SQ, CQ are configured in separate isolated panels with no unified view
3. **No visual preview** — Teachers can't see how the final paper will look before generating
4. **No mixed-source papers** — You can't combine DB questions with custom-written ones in the same paper
5. **No per-question marks editing** — MCQs are always 1 mark, no override
6. **Flat question list** — No visual sections like "Part A: MCQ (30 marks)" and "Part B: Short Questions (20 marks)"

### The Solution: A Visual Paper Canvas

Think of it like building a **Notion document** or a **Google Forms** — but specifically designed for exam papers.

#### Core Experience

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  📋 PAPER BUILDER                                    [Preview]  │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                 │
│  📝 Paper Title: "Half Yearly Exam 2026"    ⏱ 180 min          │
│  📚 Class: নবম    📖 Subject: পদার্থবিজ্ঞান                       │
│                                                                 │
│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐      │
│  │ SECTION A: বহুনির্বাচনি (MCQ)            30 marks    │      │
│  │ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────  │      │
│  │ ≡ 1. S-এর ইলেকট্রন বিন্যাস কোনটি?    [1 mark] [✕]  │      │
│  │ ≡ 2. নিচের কোনটি সঠিক?               [1 mark] [✕]   │      │
│  │ ≡ 3. পানি কোন ধরণের যৌগ?              [1 mark] [✕]   │      │
│  │    ...                                                │      │
│  │ [+ Add from Bank] [+ Write New] [+ AI Generate]      │      │
│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘      │
│                                                                 │
│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐      │
│  │ SECTION B: সংক্ষিপ্ত প্রশ্ন (SQ)         20 marks   │      │
│  │ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────  │      │
│  │ ≡ 1. তড়িৎ প্রবাহ কাকে বলে?           [2 marks] [✕]  │      │
│  │ ≡ 2. নিউটনের তৃতীয় সূত্রটি লিখ        [2 marks] [✕]  │      │
│  │ [+ Add from Bank] [+ Write New]                       │      │
│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘      │
│                                                                 │
│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐      │
│  │ SECTION C: সৃজনশীল প্রশ্ন (CQ)          50 marks    │      │
│  │ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────  │      │
│  │ ≡ 1. [উদ্দীপক preview...]              [10 marks] [✕] │      │
│  │ [+ Add from Bank] [+ Write New]                       │      │
│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘      │
│                                                                 │
│  [+ Add New Section]                                            │
│                                                                 │
│  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════             │
│  Total: 100 marks │ 30 MCQ + 10 SQ + 5 CQ                      │
│  [💾 Save Draft] [👁 Preview] [📄 Generate PDF] [📝 Generate DOCX] │
│                                                                 │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

#### Key Interactions

| Interaction | How It Works |
|-------------|-------------|
| **Drag to reorder** | Grip handle (≡) on each question — drag up/down within a section |
| **Drag between sections** | Move a question from MCQ section to SQ section (if compatible) |
| **Add from Bank** | Opens a side panel/modal to browse & search the Question Bank, click to add |
| **Write New** | Inline form to write a new question directly in the canvas |
| **AI Generate** | Opens AI generator (existing [ai_generator.py](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/utils/ai_generator.py)) scoped to the current section |
| **Remove** | Click ✕ to remove a question (returns it to the bank pool) |
| **Edit marks** | Click the marks badge to change per-question marks |
| **Section config** | Click section header to configure "Answer N out of M" rules |
| **Live totals** | Bottom bar auto-calculates total marks and question counts |
| **Preview** | Side panel shows a mini-render of the paper as it would appear in PDF |

---

## Step-by-Step Implementation Plan

### Phase 1: Backend API Extensions (3-4 days)

#### Step 1.1: New API Endpoint — Search & Fetch Questions for Builder

The builder needs a rich question fetch endpoint that returns full question data across types.

**File**: [main.py](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/routes/main.py)

```
POST /api/builder/questions
Body: {
    "chapter_ids": [1,2,3],
    "question_types": ["mcq", "sq", "cq"],  // filter by type
    "search": "তড়িৎ",                       // optional text search
    "difficulty": "medium",                  // optional
    "page": 1,
    "per_page": 20
}
Response: {
    "mcq": [{ id, question_text, type, options, difficulty, chapter_name }],
    "sq": [{ id, question_text, marks, chapter_name }],
    "cq": [{ id, stem, parts, total_marks, chapter_name }],
    "total_counts": { "mcq": 120, "sq": 45, "cq": 18 }
}
```

> [!NOTE]
> This extends the existing `/get-questions-for-chapters` endpoint but returns richer data including SQ and CQ in one call.

#### Step 1.2: New API Endpoint — Generate Paper from Builder JSON

The builder constructs a complete paper structure and sends it for generation.

**File**: [main.py](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/routes/main.py)

```
POST /api/builder/generate
Body: {
    "paper_config": {
        "title": "Half Yearly 2026",
        "class_id": 5,
        "subject_id": 12,
        "time_minutes": 180,
        "omr_style": true
    },
    "sections": [
        {
            "type": "mcq",
            "title": "বহুনির্বাচনি",
            "answer_count": 30,    // answer N out of M
            "marks_per_question": 1,
            "questions": [
                { "source": "db", "id": 101 },
                { "source": "db", "id": 102 },
                { "source": "custom", "question_text": "...", "options": [...], "correct_answer": "..." }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "sq",
            "title": "সংক্ষিপ্ত প্রশ্ন",
            "answer_count": 5,
            "marks_per_question": 2,
            "questions": [
                { "source": "db", "id": 201 },
                { "source": "custom", "question_text": "..." }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "cq",
            "title": "সৃজনশীল প্রশ্ন",
            "answer_count": 5,
            "questions": [
                { "source": "db", "id": 301 }
            ]
        }
    ]
}
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This is a new endpoint that replaces `generate-paper` and `generate-custom-paper` with a unified, section-aware generation flow. The existing endpoints remain for backward compatibility.

#### Step 1.3: Extend Document Generators

**Files**:
- [document_generator.py](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/utils/document_generator.py)
- [pdf_generator.py](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/utils/pdf_generator.py)

Add a new function `generate_paper_from_sections(sections, paper_config)` that accepts the structured sections format and renders them with proper section headers, numbering, and mixed DB + custom questions.

---

### Phase 2: Frontend — Paper Canvas UI (5-7 days)

#### Step 2.1: Create New Template `builder.html`

**File**: `app/templates/main/builder.html` [NEW]

> This is a new page at `/builder` route, separate from the existing `/generate` page. The old page stays for backward compatibility / quick generation.

Structure:
```
├── Paper Config Bar (title, class, subject, time — sticky top)
├── Sections Container (sortable)
│   ├── Section Card (MCQ)
│   │   ├── Section Header (title, marks, answer config)
│   │   ├── Question List (sortable within section)
│   │   │   └── Question Card (question text, marks badge, drag handle, delete)
│   │   └── Add Actions Bar (Add from Bank, Write New, AI Generate)
│   ├── Section Card (SQ) — same structure
│   └── Section Card (CQ) — same structure
├── Add Section Button
└── Summary Bar (total marks, counts, generate buttons)
```

#### Step 2.2: Implement Drag & Drop with SortableJS

Use [SortableJS](https://sortablejs.github.io/Sortable/) (lightweight, no jQuery dependency, 8KB gzipped).

- **Within sections**: Drag questions up/down to reorder
- **Between sections**: Drag a question from one section to another (with type compatibility check)
- **Section reordering**: Drag entire sections to change section order

```html
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/sortablejs@1.15.0/Sortable.min.js"></script>
```

#### Step 2.3: Build the Question Bank Side Panel

A slide-in panel (right side, 400px wide) that opens when "Add from Bank" is clicked:

```
┌──────────────────────────┐
│ 📚 Question Bank          │
│ ─────────────────────────│
│ 🔍 [Search questions...] │
│ Chapter: [All ▼]          │
│ Difficulty: [All ▼]       │
│ ─────────────────────────│
│ ☐ Q: তড়িৎ প্রবাহ কাকে...  │
│   Chapter 3 • Easy • ★4.2 │
│                    [+ Add] │
│ ─────────────────────────│
│ ☐ Q: নিউটনের সূত্র লিখ... │
│   Chapter 1 • Medium      │
│                    [+ Add] │
│ ─────────────────────────│
│ Load More...               │
└──────────────────────────┘
```

#### Step 2.4: Live Preview Panel

A collapsible right panel or modal that shows a mini paper preview:
- Renders the paper layout as it would appear in PDF
- Updates in real-time as questions are added/removed/reordered
- Uses CSS to mimic the PDF layout (two columns for MCQ, single column for CQ, etc.)

#### Step 2.5: Section Management

- **Add Section**: Button to add a new blank section with type selector (MCQ/SQ/CQ/Custom)
- **Section Config**: Modal to set section title, "answer N out of M" rules, marks per question
- **Delete Section**: With confirmation and option to move questions to another section
- **Auto-totals**: JavaScript calculates total marks in real-time and shows in the footer bar

---

### Phase 3: State Management & Draft Saving (2-3 days)

#### Step 3.1: Client-Side State Manager

Build a lightweight JavaScript state manager (no framework needed):

```javascript
const PaperState = {
    config: { title, class_id, subject_id, time_minutes, omr_style },
    sections: [
        {
            id: 'section_1', type: 'mcq', title: '...', 
            answer_count: 30, marks_per_question: 1,
            questions: [{ source: 'db', id: 101, text: '...' }, ...]
        },
        ...
    ],
    
    addQuestion(sectionId, question) { ... },
    removeQuestion(sectionId, questionId) { ... },
    reorder(sectionId, oldIndex, newIndex) { ... },
    moveBetweenSections(fromSection, toSection, questionId) { ... },
    getTotalMarks() { ... },
    toJSON() { ... },     // for sending to backend
    saveDraft() { ... },  // localStorage persistence
    loadDraft() { ... },
};
```

#### Step 3.2: Auto-Save to LocalStorage

- Save state to `localStorage` every 30 seconds and on every change
- On page load, check for existing draft and offer to restore
- Show "Draft saved" indicator in the UI

#### Step 3.3: Save Draft to Server (Optional, for logged-in users)

- Add a `PaperDraft` model to save work-in-progress papers server-side
- API: `POST /api/builder/drafts` and `GET /api/builder/drafts`
- Dashboard shows drafts with "Continue Editing" button

---

### Phase 4: Integration & Polish (2-3 days)

#### Step 4.1: Add Builder Link to Navigation

- Add "Paper Builder" button to the existing generate page
- Add link in the dashboard sidebar/nav
- Optionally make the builder the default for logged-in users

#### Step 4.2: Connect to Existing AI Generator

- The "AI Generate" button in each section calls the existing [ai_generator.py](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/utils/ai_generator.py)
- Returns questions scoped to the current section type (MCQ/SQ/CQ)
- Teacher can review and selectively add AI questions to the canvas

#### Step 4.3: Responsive Design & Mobile

- On mobile, the side panel becomes a full-screen overlay
- Touch-friendly drag handles
- Section collapse/expand for small screens

#### Step 4.4: Keyboard Shortcuts

| Shortcut | Action |
|----------|--------|
| `Ctrl+S` | Save draft |
| `Ctrl+P` | Preview |
| `Ctrl+Enter` | Generate paper |
| `Delete` | Remove selected question |
| `Ctrl+Z` | Undo last action |

