## Key Design Decisions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> ### 1. New Page vs. Modify Existing
> **Decision**: Create a **new `/builder` route** rather than modifying the existing `/generate` page.
> 
> **Why**: The existing generate page (2779 lines of HTML) is already complex. Adding drag-drop would make it unmaintainable. A clean new page also allows A/B testing between the old and new flows.

> [!TIP]
> ### 2. SortableJS over HTML5 Drag & Drop
> **Decision**: Use [SortableJS](https://sortablejs.github.io/Sortable/) library.
>
> **Why**: Native HTML5 Drag & Drop is inconsistent across browsers and terrible on mobile. SortableJS handles cross-browser, touch, and accessibility out of the box. It's only 8KB.

> [!NOTE]
> ### 3. Backward Compatibility
> The existing `/generate` page and API endpoints (`/generate-paper`, `/generate-custom-paper`) remain untouched. The builder is an **additive** feature. The old flow continues to work for users who prefer the simpler experience.
